## Project Finance Permissions

Two permissions control the money side of projects. Both are listed under **Teams → Permissions** in the **Work** group, and an administrator can grant them to any role, including custom roles.

- **Project Finance** opens the project **Finance** tab and the [Profit tracker](/project-management/how-to-use-the-profit-tracker/).
- **Project Expenses** opens the [Expense tracker](/project-management/how-to-use-the-expense-tracker/) and lets people add, edit and delete a project's expenses, according to the **create**, **edit** and **delete** rights.

By default only Administrators and Managers have them. Members, Clients and custom roles have none until you grant them. The **own** scope covers the projects the person leads, and **all** covers every project. Clients never see project finances. The **Projects** permission does not include either of them.

## Summary

Role Permissions in Taskip ensure secure, structured access control by defining exactly what each user role can access and manage across the platform.
